## The countries of the world for retro's map view: Natural Earth 1:50m
## admin-0 (public domain) as world-atlas has them (ISC, (c) Mike
## Bostock), simplified. Generated by tools/genworld.py -- do not edit.
##
## Points are 1/100 degree (lon, lat), zigzag varints: per ring its
## point count, then the steps from the point before (from 0, 0).
##
## `retroui/mapview` draws them; an app reaches them through it
## (`latLonOf`, `cityLatLon`, the country codes) and rarely needs these
## tables itself:
##
## ```nim
## for i in 0 ..< WorldCount:
##   if worldA2[2*i .. 2*i + 1] == "OM":
##     echo worldNames[i], " ", worldLabel[2*i + 1] / WorldScale, "N"
## ```

